.TH "SVGMARKERELEMENT.ORIENT" "3JS" "March 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGMarkerElement.orient \- SVGMarkerElement: orient property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]orient\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]SVGMarkerElement\f[R] interface defines how the marker is rotated
when it is placed at its position on the shape.
It reflects the \f[CR]orient\f[R] attribute value of the corresponding
\f[CR]<marker>\f[R] element.
.PP
Unlike \f[CR]SVGMarkerElement.orientType\f[R] and
\f[CR]SVGMarkerElement.orientAngle\f[R], which provide read\-only access
to the orientation and angle, respectively, the \f[CR]orient\f[R]
property allows you to get and set the \f[CR]orient\f[R] attribute
directly as a string.
.SH VALUE
A string.
Possible values are:
.TP
\f[B]\(dqauto\(dq\f[R]
The marker is automatically rotated to follow the direction of the path
at the point where it is placed.
.TP
\f[B]\(dqauto\-start\-reverse\(dq\f[R]
If placed by \f[CR]marker\-start\f[R], the marker is oriented at an
angle 180° from the orientation that would be used if \f[CR]auto\f[R]
were specified.
For all other markers, \f[CR]auto\-start\-reverse\f[R] means the same as
\f[CR]auto\f[R].
.TP
An \f[B]<angle>\f[R] value (e.g., \f[B]\(dq45deg\(dq\f[R])
The marker is rotated by the specified angle, measured from the
horizontal.
.TP
A \f[B]<number>\f[R] value (e.g., \f[B]\(dq45\(dq\f[R])
The marker is oriented at the specified angle in degrees.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Accessing the \f[CR]orient\f[R] property
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R]
  viewBox=\(dq0 0 100 100\(dq
  width=\(dq300\(dq
  height=\(dq300\(dq
  xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq>
  <\f[B]defs\f[R]>
    <\f[B]marker\f[R]
      id=\(dqarrow\(dq
      viewBox=\(dq0 0 10 10\(dq
      refX=\(dq5\(dq
      refY=\(dq5\(dq
      markerWidth=\(dq12\(dq
      markerHeight=\(dq12\(dq
      orient=\(dqauto\-start\-reverse\(dq>
      <\f[B]path\f[R] d=\(dqM 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\(dq />
    </\f[B]marker\f[R]>
  </\f[B]defs\f[R]>
  <\f[B]polyline\f[R]
    points=\(dq10,90 50,10 90,90\(dq
    fill=\(dqnone\(dq
    stroke=\(dqblack\(dq
    marker\-start=\(dqurl(#arrow)\(dq
    marker\-mid=\(dqurl(#arrow)\(dq
    marker\-end=\(dqurl(#arrow)\(dq />
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
<\f[B]output\f[R]></\f[B]output\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
We can read the \f[CR]orient\f[R] property and then set it to a new
value:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] marker = document.querySelector(\(dqmarker\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.querySelector(\(dqoutput\(dq);

\f[B]if\f[R] (\(dqorient\(dq \f[B]in\f[R] marker) {
  \f[I]// Read the current orient value\f[R]
  log.textContent = \(gaorient: \(dq${marker.orient}\(dq\(rsn\(ga; \f[I]// \(dqauto\-start\-reverse\(dq\f[R]

  \f[I]// Set a new orient value\f[R]
  marker.orient = \(dq90deg\(dq;
  log.textContent += \(gaafter setting \(dq90deg\(dq: \(dq${marker.orient}\(dq\(ga;
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  log.textContent = \(dqorient is not supported in this browser\(dq;
}
.EE
